// ═══ CREATING VIRTUAL THREADS (Java 21) ═══
// One virtual thread per task — simple blocking code!
Thread vt = Thread.ofVirtual().start(() -> {
    String result = httpGet("https://api.bank.com/balance");  // BLOCKS — but cheap!
    // JVM unmounts this virtual thread from carrier → carrier free!
});

// ExecutorService with virtual threads:
try (var executor = Executors.newVirtualThreadPerTaskExecutor()) {
    for (int i = 0; i < 100_000; i++) {
        executor.submit(() -> {
            dbQuery("SELECT balance ...");  // blocking IO — but virtual thread!
            // 100K virtual threads, each blocking → all on ~4 carrier threads!
        });
    }
}
// 100K concurrent requests with simple blocking code! No async needed!

// ═══ WHAT VIRTUAL THREADS REPLACE ═══
// BEFORE (platform threads + @Async):
@Async  // Spring creates platform thread per call — limited to pool size!
public CompletableFuture<Balance> getBalance(String id) {
    return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> repository.findById(id), asyncPool);
}
// Complex: @Async annotation, custom pool config, CF wrapping

// AFTER (virtual threads):
public Balance getBalance(String id) {
    return repository.findById(id);  // simple blocking call!
}
// Called from virtual thread → blocking is FREE! No @Async, no CF, no pool tuning!

// ═══ WHAT CF STILL DOES BETTER ═══
// 1. Composing independent parallel calls:
CompletableFuture<Void> all = CompletableFuture.allOf(
    supplyAsync(() -> getBalance()),
    supplyAsync(() -> getCreditScore()),
    supplyAsync(() -> getPropertyValue())
);
// Virtual threads: you'd need to manually start 3 threads + join them.
// CF: cleaner composition with allOf/anyOf/thenCombine.

// 2. Timeouts and fallbacks:
cf.orTimeout(5, TimeUnit.SECONDS)
  .exceptionally(ex -> fallbackValue);
// Virtual threads: no built-in timeout/fallback pipeline.

// ═══ WHAT PLATFORM POOLS STILL DO BETTER ═══
// CPU-bound work: virtual threads on carrier pool (few threads)
// → same as platform threads! No speedup!
// Parallel computation needs ALL cores busy:
data.parallelStream().map(this::heavyCompute).sum();  // ForkJoinPool — platform threads!
// Virtual threads: blocking IO = efficient. CPU-bound = no advantage.

// ═══ SUMMARY ═══
// IO-bound fan-out:        virtual threads (Recommended) (simple blocking code)
// Compose/combine/timeout:  CompletableFuture (Recommended) (thenCombine, allOf, orTimeout)
// CPU-bound parallelism:    platform thread pool (Recommended) (ForkJoinPool, parallelStream)
// "Async is dead":          OVERSTATEMENT — CF composition still unmatched
